{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid _print(const char *sdbg, long long h) { cerr<<sdbg<<'='<<h<<'\\n'; }\ntemplate<typename... Args>\nvoid _print(const char *sdbg, long long h, Args... rest) {\n  for(; *sdbg != ','; ++sdbg) cerr << *sdbg;\n  cerr << '=' << h << ',';\n  _print(sdbg + 1, rest...);\n}\ntemplate<typename T>\nostream& operator<<(ostream& os, const vector<T>& v) {\n  os << '[';\n  for(const auto& x : v) os << x << ',';\n  return os << ']';\n}\ntemplate<typename L, typename R>\nostream& operator<<(ostream& os, const pair<L,R>& p) {\n  return os << '(' << p.first << ',' << p.second << ')';\n}\n#define trace(...) _print(#__VA_ARGS__, __VA_ARGS__)\n\nvector<long long> rep;\nlong long calc(long long x, long long pos) {\n  long long q = x / rep[pos];\n  x %= rep[pos];\n  if(x == 0) return q * pos;\n  return q * pos + min(pos + calc(rep[pos] - x, pos - 1), calc(x, pos - 1));\n}\nint main() {\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false); cin.tie(nullptr);\n  \n  long long t = 1, n;\n  long long val = 0;\n  while(rep.size() < 17) {\n    rep.push_back(val);\n    val = val * 10 + 1;\n  }\n  while(t--) {\n    cin >> n;\n    cout << calc(n, 16);\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef _print(sdbg, h, *rest):\n    import sys\n    if rest:\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(sdbg) and sdbg[i] != ',':\n            sys.stderr.write(sdbg[i])\n            i += 1\n        sys.stderr.write('=' + str(h) + ',')\n        _print(sdbg[i+1:] if i < len(sdbg) else '', *rest)\n    else:\n        sys.stderr.write(sdbg + '=' + str(h) + '\\n')\n\ndef calc(x, pos, rep):\n    q = x // rep[pos]\n    x %= rep[pos]\n    if x == 0:\n        return q * pos\n    return q * pos + min(pos + calc(rep[pos] - x, pos - 1, rep), calc(x, pos - 1, rep))\n\ndef main():\n    rep = []\n    val = 0\n    while len(rep) < 17:\n        rep.append(val)\n        val = val * 10 + 1\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    t = int(data[0])\n    index = 1\n    results = []\n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n        results.append(str(calc(n, 16, rep)))\n    \n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001586549769854173, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -0.12699387967586517, -3.8742269680369645e-05, -0.10020884871482849, -0.0022088908590376377, -0.0021828413009643555, -3.504691630951129e-05, -0.00014625910262111574, -8.05822346592322e-05, -3.6954195820726454e-05, -0.16029630601406097, -0.25194600224494934, -1.1205610462639015e-05, -0.08895733952522278, -2.264974000354414e-06, -3.421248038648628e-05, -0.606627345085144, -0.08796710520982742, -1.6212332411669195e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.014580721035599709, -0.31603506207466125, -5.173549288883805e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.738841712474823, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.19886